## Summary

✅ **DO:**
- Use ng2-charts or Chart.js with Angular
- Define chart data with Angular Signals
- Use OnPush change detection
- Format data with pure functions
- Make charts responsive with fixed height containers
- Include accessibility attributes
- Use component classes (`.card`) with utility classes for layout

❌ **DON'T:**
- Use React hooks (useState, useMemo, useEffect)
- Use `className` - use `class` in Angular
- Skip accessibility considerations
- Hardcode colors - use design tokens
- Forget to handle loading/error states
- Use inline styles for charts - use CSS classes
